cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite the accompanying paper."
title: "Dissemination-aware weather forecast vintages for day-ahead electricity price forecasting in Japan"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Okauchi"
    given-names: "Ryota"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-5391-7133"
    affiliation: "The University of Tokyo"
    website: "https://github.com/R-Okauchi"
  - family-names: "Chun"
    given-names: "Pang-jo"
    affiliation: "The University of Tokyo"
abstract: >-
  Reproduction companion for a study of how the DISSEMINATION time of a weather
  forecast -- not its initialisation time -- determines what that forecast is
  worth in a day-ahead electricity market. On the Japan Electric Power Exchange,
  archive write times over 2,189 delivery days from 2020 to 2026 show that no
  file of the previous-day 00 UTC meso-scale run reached the archive before the
  10:00 JST gate, as JMA's documented observation cut-off and job schedule also
  imply, while the runs initialised two days before delivery arrived in time on
  every audited day. The repository carries one script per analysis phase --
  the dissemination-correct ladder of run-pinned tiers, the 2021-2024 backcast
  that spans Japan's scarcity-price episodes, the learner-strength and
  robustness families, and the dissemination audit -- a frozen provenance JSON
  per phase, and a drift guard that re-derives every headline quantity in the
  manuscript from that provenance without needing raw data.
keywords:
  - electricity price forecasting
  - forecast vintage
  - gate closure
  - dissemination time
  - value of information
  - numerical weather prediction
  - solar curtailment
  - price floor
  - JEPX
  - forecast evaluation
  - pre-registration
version: "v0.2.1"
date-released: "2026-10-24"
